&lt;h2&gt;


🤭 Fun
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://x.com/awesomekling/status/2079559664249819452" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fthisweekinreact.com%2Femails%2Fissues%2F292%2Fmeme.jpg" alt="alt"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;See ya! 👋&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hi everyone, &lt;a href="https://x.com/sebastienlorber" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Seb&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://x.com/jaworek3211" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Jan&lt;/a&gt; here 👋!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This week we have an interesting React challenger, keeping its mental model but compiled ahead of time. Also various major announcements from the TanStack side.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On the mobile side, we have interesting RN 0.87 PRs to look at, discussions around workers / worklets, a WebGPU/Skia integration, and React Navigation 8 / Screens 5 progress.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Last week, many proposals progressed during a TC39 meeting. npm is going to scan for malware at publish time. Core Web Vitals will now measure SPA soft navigation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let's dive in!&lt;/p&gt;




